<title>USA: Georgia sees 6,250 drop in jobless claims in May.</title>
<headline>Georgia sees 6,250 drop in jobless claims in May.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people drawing unemployment benefits in Georgia declined by 6,250 from April to May, state Labor Commissioner David Poythress said.</p>
<p>In May, 40,834 workers drew $18.7 million in benefits, compared with 47,078 workers who drew $23.5 million in benefits in May last year.</p>
<p>Most of the monthly decrease in jobless claims was due to strengthening trade and services, especially outdoor sectors such as construction and agriculture. Most of the yearly decrease in claims was in manufacturing, Poythress said.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
